### gaji-engine — manual requests
### Open this file in IntelliJ IDEA and press the green play button on any block.
### No plugin needed: IntelliJ's built-in HTTP Client handles it.
### Requires the app running on localhost:8080.

@host = http://localhost:8080

### ---------------------------------------------------------------
### JP wage cap, January 2026 — still the 2025 figure
### Expect wageCap 10547400, validTo 2026-03-01
### ---------------------------------------------------------------
GET {{host}}/api/v1/rules/jp-cap?date=2026-01-15

### ---------------------------------------------------------------
### JP wage cap, last day before the March change
### Expect the SAME cap as January: 10547400
### ---------------------------------------------------------------
GET {{host}}/api/v1/rules/jp-cap?date=2026-02-28

### ---------------------------------------------------------------
### JP wage cap, April 2026 — the new figure, one day into the new rule
### Expect wageCap 11086300, validTo null
### Same salary, same year, different correct answer.
### ---------------------------------------------------------------
GET {{host}}/api/v1/rules/jp-cap?date=2026-04-15

### ---------------------------------------------------------------
### Same request three years earlier
### Expect wageCap 9559600
### ---------------------------------------------------------------
GET {{host}}/api/v1/rules/jp-cap?date=2023-06-01

### ---------------------------------------------------------------
### A date with no rules at all
### Expect HTTP 400 with code NO_RULE_FOR_DATE — refusing to guess
### ---------------------------------------------------------------
GET {{host}}/api/v1/rules/jp-cap?date=2019-05-01

### ---------------------------------------------------------------
### Malformed date
### Expect HTTP 400 with code INVALID_PARAMETER
### ---------------------------------------------------------------
GET {{host}}/api/v1/rules/jp-cap?date=15-01-2026

### ---------------------------------------------------------------
### PTKP, married with one dependent
### Expect amount 63000000
### ---------------------------------------------------------------
GET {{host}}/api/v1/rules/ptkp?date=2026-06-01&status=K/1

### ---------------------------------------------------------------
### PTKP, single with no dependents
### Expect amount 54000000
### ---------------------------------------------------------------
GET {{host}}/api/v1/rules/ptkp?date=2026-06-01&status=TK/0

### ---------------------------------------------------------------
### PTKP with a status that does not exist
### Expect HTTP 400 — not a silent zero
### ---------------------------------------------------------------
GET {{host}}/api/v1/rules/ptkp?date=2026-06-01&status=K/9

### ---------------------------------------------------------------
### TER — the worked example from PP 58/2023 itself
### Rp10.000.000 gross, PTKP K/0, table A layer 9
### Expect category A, rate 0.02, withholding 200000
### ---------------------------------------------------------------
GET {{host}}/api/v1/rules/ter?date=2026-06-01&status=K/0&gross=10000000

### ---------------------------------------------------------------
### Same gross, different PTKP status — different category, different tax
### K/3 uses table C
### ---------------------------------------------------------------
GET {{host}}/api/v1/rules/ter?date=2026-06-01&status=K/3&gross=10000000

### ---------------------------------------------------------------
### Income below the first layer
### Expect rate 0 and withholding 0
### ---------------------------------------------------------------
GET {{host}}/api/v1/rules/ter?date=2026-06-01&status=TK/0&gross=5000000

### ---------------------------------------------------------------
### One rupiah across a layer boundary (layer 8 -> layer 9)
### 9650000 -> 1.75%   |   9650001 -> 2.00%
### ---------------------------------------------------------------
GET {{host}}/api/v1/rules/ter?date=2026-06-01&status=TK/0&gross=9650000

###
GET {{host}}/api/v1/rules/ter?date=2026-06-01&status=TK/0&gross=9650001

### ===============================================================
### CALCULATION — POST /api/v1/calculate
### ===============================================================

### ---------------------------------------------------------------
### January 2026 — PPh 21 uses TER
### JHT 200.000 | JP 100.000 | Kesehatan 100.000 | PPh21 200.000
### Take home 9.400.000
### ---------------------------------------------------------------
POST {{host}}/api/v1/calculate
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "grossMonthly": 10000000,
  "ptkpStatus": "K/0",
  "period": "2026-01-01"
}

### ---------------------------------------------------------------
### December 2026 — same person, same salary, annual reconciliation
### PPh21 is 515.000, not 200.000. This matches PP 58/2023's own
### worked example exactly. The "december" block shows every step.
### ---------------------------------------------------------------
POST {{host}}/api/v1/calculate
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "grossMonthly": 10000000,
  "ptkpStatus": "K/0",
  "period": "2026-12-01"
}

### ---------------------------------------------------------------
### January vs April 2026 — the March JP cap change
### JP is 105.474 in January and 110.863 in April. Everything else
### about the two payslips is identical.
### ---------------------------------------------------------------
POST {{host}}/api/v1/calculate
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "grossMonthly": 12000000,
  "ptkpStatus": "K/0",
  "period": "2026-01-15"
}

###
POST {{host}}/api/v1/calculate
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "grossMonthly": 12000000,
  "ptkpStatus": "K/0",
  "period": "2026-04-15"
}

### ---------------------------------------------------------------
### A date before TER existed
### Expect HTTP 400 NO_RULE_FOR_DATE — the engine will not guess
### ---------------------------------------------------------------
POST {{host}}/api/v1/calculate
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "grossMonthly": 10000000,
  "ptkpStatus": "K/0",
  "period": "2023-06-01"
}
